Occasionally, a question pops up on this newsgroup as to who is
the Development Team "and what does Finland have to do with it..".

The answer is in the 'history' file, the 'Install.*' files, and in
other places in the code where credit is gratefully acknowledged.

I suppose that a person in the US who sends a msg to nethack-bugs
might be surprised when the response to his/her msg comes from Finland,
or from Sweden, or from West Germany, or from France, or from Canada.

There shouldn't be a surprise.  The Development Team is an international
team, literally.  Mail sent to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu is
automatically distributed to all the members of the Development Team --
wherever they are.  Unless the content of the mail requires group
discussion, it is answered by whoever has the most ready answer.  And the
answer is also circulated through nethack-bugs, so that all of us are
made aware of its content.  

-Izchak


